  "abstract": "RepFusion repurposes a frozen multimodal LLM as a noisy representation encoder for text-to-image diffusion in Representation Autoencoder space. Instead of using the LLM only once as a static text encoder, it feeds the evolving noisy RAE latent into the MLLM at each denoising step, then uses the token-aligned MLLM outputs to condition a DiT via AdaLN-Single. The paper shows that noisy representation input, RAE latents, and preserved multimodal perception priors improve prompt alignment under controlled compute comparisons.",
